From 24e7d7846d97b979f391fb4869983a8ae3b9fd36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: m5agent <m5agent@m5stack.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 20:57:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hw/m5stopwatch: add Unit batch-3 C data planes

Add the four remaining batch-3 C Units as controller-visible models,
following docs/unit-research/2026-11-02-batch3-protocols.md. No guest
evidence is recorded; host catalog keeps all four planned.

- env-iv (U001-D): new US_SHT4X slave at 0x44 (command byte, 6-byte
  temperature/humidity or serial frame with per-word CRC8 poly 0x31) plus the
  existing US_BMP280 at 0x76 via the 0126 multi-slave attach. The snapshot
  SHT4x driver getters are broken (self.measure[0/1] without call), so the
  model returns spec-correct frames and the host must anchor the fixed master
  driver SHA.
- co2 (U103): new US_SCD40 slave at 0x62 implementing the SCD4x command +
  CRC-word protocol: 2-byte BE commands, set-argument commands with value+CRC,
  data-ready/measurement/temperature-offset/altitude/serial/self-test response
  words, and start/stop/reinit/single-shot state transitions. The snapshot
  asyncio driver vs master sync rewrite and SCD40-vs-SCD41 identity stay
  UNRESOLVED. Note: both driver versions decode temperature from buf[1]
  instead of buf[4], so guest temperature decode remains a documented driver
  bug; CO2 and humidity are assertable.
- pbhub (U041): CONTROL_PBHUB at 0x61. The official driver always talks to the
  single hub address and passes channel_base|offset as the register byte, so
  the six channels (bases 0x40/0x50/0x60/0x70/0x80/0xA0, offsets 0x00..0x0B)
  live in one 256-byte command space rather than on separate bus addresses.
  Digital/analog/RGB/servo/brightness writes update per-channel QOM state; the
  0xFA RGB mode register and 0xFF address migration follow the pinned master
  driver (wire RGB is GRB); reads return fixture inputs. MCU identity
  (MEGA328 vs STM32F030F4P6) and channel-address overlap with registered
  Units remain catalog blockers.
- ultrasonic-io (U098-B2): GPIO branch that observes the guest trigger edge on
  yellow and drives a white echo pulse of distance_mm*582/100 us; out-of-range
  distances withhold the echo so the guest sees a real timeout instead of a
  fabricated value. MicroPython time_pulse_us timeout semantics stay
  UNRESOLVED.

Offline QOM smoke (no guest firmware) validates property registration, fixture
read/write, range rejection, read-only rejection and the env-iv dual-slave
children; it is not a functional PASS.
